  "notes": "\"R\" variant has all 24 RJ45 ports and the 2 SFP uplink ports rear-facing (vs \"F\" variant front-facing); electrically identical. Confirmed via Araknis/SnapAV Quick Start Guide (manufacturer) and cross-checked against SnapAV product page and AV-iQ spec listing. All 24 RJ45 ports are Gigabit (1000BASE-T) and support PoE/PoE+ (802.3af/at), with a total PoE power budget of 375W (30W max per port). The 2 SFP ports are 1000BASE-X (Gigabit) uplinks accepting Araknis SFP-to-RJ45 or multi-mode fiber adapters (modeled here as bidirectional RJ45-grade ports since no fiber connector ID exists in the allowed list other than fiber-lc/sfp; used \"rj45\" with eth-1g grade to represent the copper-SFP use case is not ideal, so ports are listed as sfp connector without grade per rules... see note). No console/RS232 management port is documented. Power input is a standard IEC C14 inlet with a detachable AC power cord (100-240V, 50/60Hz per AV-iQ; QSG shows 120V AC in the connection diagram, but the switch itself is a standard IEC-input device compatible with worldwide voltages per the C14 inlet). No dimensions/weight independently verified beyond one secondary source (17.32in x 1.73in x 16.14in from SnapAV shop page paraphrase).",
